  "description": "London Borough of Lambeth No. 185 (Christchurch Road, Garden Lane, SW2) Tree Preservation Order 1987.  T1 Lime, G1 2 Limes and 1 Horse Chestnut  and G2 4 Limes .\r\rThe following tree references correspond with the applicant's submitted tree location plan.\rT5 Lime - Rear garden of 12 Claremont Close. Crown lift to 4m above ground level.\rT6 Lime - Rear garden of 13 Claremont Close. Crown lift to 4m above ground level.\rT7 Lime - Rear garden of 13 Claremont Close. Crown lift to 4m above ground level and remove deadwood.\rT8 Lime - Rear garden of 14 Claremont Close. Remove epicormic growth encroaching into the garden and against the boundary fence. Remove deadwood.\rT9 Lime - Side of 14 Claremont Close. Shorten epicormic growth by 1m towards the boundary wall to reduce overhang of the footpath.\r\rOther submitted works\rT1 and T2 Ash - Reduce height by 3m from 15m to 12m. T3 Oak - Reduce laterally by 2m away from the building. T4 Ash - Reduce height by 4m from 10m to 6m and reduce laterally by 2m away from the building. T10 Holm oak - Reduce laterally by 2m over the pavement.\r\rCouncil Note: \rThe applicant's tree references differ from the statutory Order references. The proposed scope of consent is identified in Sections 2 and 7.",
